# Performance (caveman)

- Cache hot data with Laravel cache helpers.
- Use queue for heavy tasks.
- Avoid N+1: eager load relations.
- Use indexes when query pattern needs.
- Multi-DB compatibility (MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQLite): see `09-database-guidelines.mdc` and `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-database-guidelines-design.md`.
- Use transactions for multi-step consistency.
- Keep DB compatibility (MySQL/Postgres/SQLite/Oracle where possible or add comment if not).
- Prefer Eloquent/query builder abstractions over vendor-specific SQL.

## Large datasets

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Small known set (< ~500), full Collection | `get()` |
| Iterate all, may need `with()` | `lazy(n)` |
| Per-batch side effects | `chunk(n)` |
| Huge simple scan, no relations | `cursor()` — no `with()` |
| API infinite scroll | `cursorPaginate()` + unique `orderBy` |
| One row | `first()` / `limit(1)` |

- `cursor()` never with `with()` — N+1 risk.
- Spec backlog: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-large-dataset-query-patterns-design.md`.

## Filament tables

- Eager load every relation used in columns, filters, or `formatStateUsing`.
- Always `defaultSort()`; keep pagination (~25), no `paginated(false)` on growing tables.
- Cache heavy filter option queries (short TTL) or use `relationship()->preload()`.
- Widget stats: prefer `$isLazy = true` and/or short cache.
- Checklist detail: same spec file, Filament section.

- For deep Laravel perf patterns: see `laravel-boost.mdc`.
